                "text_en": "To: All Receiving and Outbound Dock Staff\nFrom: Tariq Mansour, Warehouse Operations Manager\nDate: October 18\nSubject: Transition to 2D QR Pallet Labels\n\nStarting Monday, October 25, our fulfillment center [[blank:ag-i-p6-000401-1]] traditional linear barcodes with high-density 2D QR labels on all outbound freight pallets. Unlike older labels that stored only a seven-digit SKU, the new QR format encodes batch numbers, expiration dates, and destination bay codes in a single scan.\n\nAll handheld scanners in Dock Zones 1 through 4 have already received the firmware update needed to read the new labels. [[blank:ag-i-p6-000401-2]] Simply place the scanner in its charging cradle for ten minutes if the screen prompts for a restart.\n\nDuring the first week of the transition, incoming shipments from legacy suppliers may still arrive with linear barcodes. [[blank:ag-i-p6-000401-3]], the updated scanners remain backward-compatible and will process both label styles without manual switching. Please direct any technical [[blank:ag-i-p6-000401-4]] to Lead Technician Clara Gomez at extension 4409."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
